    {
        key = "getting-started", src = "bnb-6ad64115eabc3964", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = nil,
        title = "Getting started",
        body = "{p}BigNoteBox is a notepad inside the game. Your notes are kept for your whole account, and each one belongs to every character (Global) or to one character.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Open it{/h3}\n- Type /bnb, press Ctrl+N, or click the minimap button {icon:@icon:16}.\n- F8 makes a new note, F7 a quick note: {link*bnbui:help.quick-notes*Quick notes}.\n- Ctrl+Space opens {link*bnbui:help.oracle-search*Oracle search} from anywhere.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Find your notes{/h3}\n{p}The main window shows your notes in one of two ways, and the icon at the top left switches between them:{/p}\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-explorer-mode:16} The {link*bnbui:help.explorer-view*Explorer view}: your notes and folders as a grid of icons over the whole window, like the file explorer on your computer.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-list-mode:16} The {link*bnbui:help.note-list*Note list}: a list on the left, the open note on the right.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Write{/h3}\n{p}Open a note and write: {link*bnbui:help.writing-notes*Writing notes}. A new note can start from a {link*bnbui:help.note-templates*template}.{/p}\n{h3}Choose what you use{/h3}\n{p}Most parts of BigNoteBox are modules you can switch on or off: {link*bnbui:help.modules*Modules}. The {link*bnbui:wizard*setup wizard} sets them up for you.{/p}\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} Right-click almost anything for more choices: a note, a folder, a link, empty space.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "note-list", src = "bnb-6ad64115aba01ebb", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "finding-your-notes",
        title = "Note list",
        body = "{p}The list on the left of the main window, beside the open note. The icon {icon:@Explorer/ex-explorer-mode:16} left of the sort dropdown switches to the {link*bnbui:help.explorer-view*Explorer view}. From top to bottom:{/p}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-pinned:16} Pinned: the notes you pinned (right-click > Pin to top).\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-folder:16} Your folders: {link*bnbui:help.folders*Folders}.\n- Notes: everything else, in the sort you picked.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Find a note{/h3}\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-search:16} The search box finds text in titles and notes as you type.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-favorite:16} The star and {icon:@UI/ui-tasks:16} task buttons show only favorites, or notes with tasks.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-folder:16} The folder view and {icon:@UI/ui-treeview:16} tag tree buttons, left of the search box, group notes by folder or by tag.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Do things{/h3}\n- Right-click a note for everything you can do with it.\n- Hold a note and drag it: to reorder (Custom sort), or onto a folder.\n- The arrow at the top folds the list to icons only.\n{p}Character tabs beside the list show one character's notes at a time: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.sidebar*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "explorer-view", src = "bnb-6ada45417fde3bdc", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "finding-your-notes",
        title = "Explorer view",
        body = "{p}The Explorer view shows your notes and folders as a grid of icons over the whole main window, the way the file explorer on your computer shows files. The icon at the top left switches between it {icon:@Explorer/ex-explorer-mode:16} and the {link*bnbui:help.note-list*Note list} {icon:@Explorer/ex-list-mode:16}.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Open and go back{/h3}\n- Double-click a note or a folder to open it.\n- The arrow at the top left, or Esc, takes you back. Next to it is where you are: click Notes there to go back to the top.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-chevron-down:16} Pinned and Notes are headers you can fold away.\n{h3}Pick notes{/h3}\n- Click a note to pick it. Ctrl+click picks more, Shift+click picks a row of them, or drag a box around several.\n- The bar at the bottom counts your notes and folders, and what you picked.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}The buttons along the top{/h3}\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-new:16} New: a note {icon:@Explorer/ex-new-note:16} in the open folder, or a new folder {icon:@Explorer/ex-new-folder:16}.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-copy:16} Copy, {icon:@Explorer/ex-move:16} Move, {icon:@Explorer/ex-delete:16} Delete, {icon:@Explorer/ex-rename:16} Rename, {icon:@Explorer/ex-pin:16} Pin, {icon:@Explorer/ex-favorite:16} Favorite, {icon:@Explorer/ex-share:16} Share and {icon:@Explorer/ex-export:16} Export work on the notes you picked.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-sort:16} Sort and Order: how the notes are sorted.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-view:16} View: small {icon:@Explorer/ex-view-small:16}, medium {icon:@Explorer/ex-view-medium:16} or large {icon:@Explorer/ex-view-large:16} icons, a list of titles {icon:@Explorer/ex-view-list:16}, details in columns {icon:@Explorer/ex-view-details:16}, or every note in one flat list {icon:@Explorer/ex-view-flat:16}.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-search:16} The search button opens a search field; the buttons at its end show only favorites or notes with tasks.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-more:16} In a small window, the buttons that do not fit go under More.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Drag and right-click{/h3}\n- Drag notes onto a folder to file them. Drop them on Notes in the path to take them out again.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-sort-custom:16} In Custom sort, drag the icons into the order you like.\n- Right-click a note, a folder or empty space for everything else. Empty space has Sort by, New folder and the View choices, among them Pinned notes first and Favorites first.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Inside a note{/h3}\n{p}The note fills the window. The button at the right end of the toolbar opens the note menu, with Note settings {icon:@Toolbar/tb-notesettings:16} and situations; right-clicking the text has Open note settings at the bottom. The icon beside the title changes the note's icon.{/p}\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.explorer*}. There you pick which view the window opens on, and whether it opens on the note you had open when you closed it.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "folders", src = "bnb-6ad641151adf46de", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "finding-your-notes",
        title = "Folders",
        body = "{p}Folders keep notes together. They sit between Pinned and your notes, A-Z, and remember whether you left them open.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Put notes in a folder{/h3}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-folder:16} Right-click a note > Move to folder, then a folder or {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-folder-add:16} New folder...\n- Drag a note onto a folder header. Drop it on the Notes header to take it out again.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-copy-move:16} Actions > Copy / Move to... can copy or move notes into a folder too.\n- {icon:@Explorer/ex-new-folder:16} In the {link*bnbui:help.explorer-view*Explorer view}, drag notes onto a folder icon, or pick some and right-click empty space > New folder with selection.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}The folder itself{/h3}\n{p}Right-click a folder to add a note to it, rename it, give it a color or delete it. A pinned note shows under Pinned and in its folder.{/p}\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} Deleting a folder never deletes its notes: they go back under Notes.{/p}\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.folders*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "tags", src = "bnb-6ad64115c3964d38", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "finding-your-notes",
        title = "Tags",
        body = "{p}Tags are short words on a note, like Raid or Gold. A note can have as many as you like, and a tag is the same whatever its case.{/p}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-tags-add:16} Right-click a note > Add tags, or add them under the title in the editor.\n- Click a tag to show only the notes that have it.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-treeview:16} The tag tree button groups every note by tag.\n- {icon:@Topbar/Normal/tp-tagmanager-normal:16} The {link*bnbui:tagmanager*} renames, colors and deletes tags across all your notes.",
    },
    {
        key = "oracle-search", src = "bnb-6ad64115cdf93a99", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "finding-your-notes",
        title = "Oracle search",
        body = "{p}A search bar that finds any note from anywhere in the game, by title, text or tags. Open it with Ctrl+Space or /bnb search.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Open a note{/h3}\n- Enter: open it.\n- Shift: as a sticky note {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-sticky-note:16}. Ctrl: in Focus mode {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-focus-mode:16}. Alt: in the Reference Box {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-reference-box:16}.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Narrow it down{/h3}\n{p}Type a letter and a space before your words. Type ? in the bar to see them all.{/p}\n- p player notes, n NPC notes {icon:@Search/s-icon-npc:16}, i notes with an item {icon:@Search/s-icon-items:16}, z notes tied to a zone {icon:@Search/s-icon-situation:16}.\n- c this character, g global {icon:@Search/s-icon-global:16}, t tasks {icon:@Search/s-icon-tasks:16}, a alarms {icon:@Search/s-icon-alarm:16}, x rich {icon:@Search/s-icon-rich:16}, l plain.\n- d today, d week, d month: made or edited then.\n- b searches the Trash, o searches the settings, m sends a note to chat.\n- #tag, @who the note is about, * favorites, -word leaves a word out, \"an exact phrase\".\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.oracle*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "writing-notes", src = "bnb-6ad641159f064ec7", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Writing notes",
        body = "{p}The editor shows the open note: the title on top, the text below. In the Note list it is the right side of the window; in the Explorer view the note fills the window.{/p}\n- Notes save as you type. A setting can switch this to a Save button.\n- {icon:@Toolbar/tb-undo:16} Undo and {icon:@Toolbar/tb-redo:16} Redo work per note: {link*bnbui:help.history-and-undo*History and undo}.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-locked:16} A locked note cannot be changed: right-click > Lock note / Unlock note.\n- The toolbar above the text inserts waypoints {icon:@Toolbar/tb-way:16}, links {icon:@Toolbar/tb-link:16}, time stamps {icon:@Toolbar/tb-timestamp:16} and {link*bnbui:help.note-tokens*note tokens} {icon:@Toolbar/tb-syntax:16}.\n- The button at the right end of the toolbar opens the note menu: Note settings, situations, alarms, tasks and more.\n- Right-click the text to insert game info; Open note settings is at the bottom.\n- {icon:@Toolbar/tb-notesettings:16} Note settings has the note's look, icon and situation.\n{p}{icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-rich-note:16} For headings, colors and pictures, make it a {link*bnbui:help.rich-notes*rich note}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "note-templates", src = "bnb-6ada45411100f55b", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Note templates",
        body = "{p}A template fills a new note for you: a title, text, tags and a look to start from.{/p}\n{p:c}{icon:@Templates/tmp-blank:40} {icon:@Templates/tmp-boss:40} {icon:@Templates/tmp-weekly:40} {icon:@Templates/tmp-diary:40} {icon:@Templates/tmp-more:40}{/p}\n- The New Note window has Blank, Boss, Weekly and Journal at the top. More shows every template.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-save-template:16} To make your own, right-click a note > Actions > Save as template.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-share:16} A template can be shared as a code, like a note.\n{p}Rename, change or delete your templates, or copy a built-in one, in {link*bnbui:settings.notes.templates*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "rich-notes", src = "bnb-6ad64115bc710dda", rich = false, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Rich notes",
        body = "A rich note is a small page: headings, colors, icons, pictures and links. The toolbar inserts every tag for you, and the preview beside the editor shows the result as you type.\n\nRight-click a note > Convert to rich or normal note.\n\nThe tags:\n- {h1}Title{/h1}, {h2}...{/h2}, {h3}...{/h3}: headings. {h1:c} centers one, {h1:r} puts it on the right.\n- {p}text{/p}: a paragraph. {p:c} centered, {p:r} on the right.\n- {col:ff8800}text{/col}: colored text.\n- {u}text{/u}: underlined text. {s}text{/s}: struck through. The lines show in View mode and in the preview; while you edit, you see the tags.\n- {icon:INV_Misc_Note_01:16}: a game icon in the text, 16 pixels.\n- {img:path:width:height}: a picture.\n- {link*address*text}: a link. {link*bnbui:oracle*{icon:INV_Misc_Spyglass_03:16}} is a picture button that opens the Oracle bar.\n- {br}: a new line inside a paragraph.\n\nWith the Rich Notes module off, every note shows as plain text with its tags visible, like this one (Settings > Modules > Rich Notes).",
    },
    {
        key = "note-tokens", src = "bnb-6ada4541b8cff90d", rich = false, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Note tokens",
        body = "A note token is a word in double braces that BigNoteBox fills in for you. Type {{ in a note to see the list, or use the token button on the toolbar.\n\nHere and now, filled in once when you finish typing it:\n- {{date}}, {{time}}, {{datetime}}: today's date and the time.\n- {{zone}}, {{subzone}}, {{instance}}: where you are.\n- {{target}}: your target's name. {{coords}}: where you stand, as a waypoint link.\n\nYour character: {{me}}, {{name}}, {{realm}}, {{class}}, {{race}}, {{level}}, {{spec}}, {{ilvl}}, {{guild}}, {{gold}} and more. In a rich note these stay in the note and show the character of whoever reads it; in a normal note they become the value right away.\n\nGame data by id: {{item:6948}} and the like show the link. The id is the number in the thing's Wowhead address.\n\nMake tokens of your own in Settings > Notes > Tokens. ",
    },
    {
        key = "links-in-notes", src = "bnb-6ad64115e4af0721", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Links in notes",
        body = "{p}The link button {icon:@Toolbar/tb-link:16} on the editor toolbar puts a link at the cursor. Right-click any link for more choices.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Note links{/h3}\n{p}A link to another note. It keeps working when that note is renamed. If the note is deleted, the link turns gray; Shift-click it to bring the note back from the Trash.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Waypoint links{/h3}\n{p}{icon:@Toolbar/tb-way:16} A place on the map.{/p}\n- Click: place the waypoint and track it.\n- Shift-click: put the map pin into chat.\n- Ctrl-click: copy a /way line.\n- Alt-click: show it on the map.\n{p}In a rich note, a typed /way line becomes a link by itself.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}BigNoteBox links{/h3}\n{p}The link button's BigNoteBox tab links to a Settings page, a window or a help topic, like this one: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.situations*}. A rich note can make one a picture button: {link*bnbui:oracle*{icon:INV_Misc_Spyglass_03:20}} (see {link*bnbui:help.rich-notes*Rich notes}).{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "quick-notes", src = "bnb-6ad64115a6c638d1", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Quick notes",
        body = "{p}{icon:@Explorer/ex-quick-note:16} Ways to make a note in a hurry.{/p}\n- F7 makes a new note at once, in the main window or as a sticky note to type in.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-icon-quest:16} Quest, gossip, book and letter windows get a note button: one click makes a note of what they say.\n- {icon:@BCB/addon-dialogueui:16} Dialogue UI and {icon:@BCB/addon-immersion:16} Immersion get the same button.\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.quickNote*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "focus-mode", src = "bnb-6ad64115416c83a7", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Focus mode",
        body = "{p}{icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-focus-mode:16} Write in full screen, with the game interface hidden and the camera slowly turning around your character.{/p}\n- Open it from the editor toolbar, or with Ctrl+Enter in the Oracle bar.\n- A rich note gets its preview beside the text.\n- Esc or the close button brings everything back as it was.\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.focus*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "spelling", src = "bnb-6addf7de55d5d478", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Spelling",
        body = "{p}BigNoteBox can mark words that are not in the dictionary with a red wavy line while you write. It never changes a word for you: you decide what to fix.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Switching it on{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:settings.modules.spelling*} has the switch. It is on by default when your game is in English.\n- Language: English (US) or English (UK). These come with the addon.\n- When to check: as you type, or only when you click Check spelling {icon:@Toolbar/tb-spellcheck:16} in the formatting toolbar.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}What it leaves alone{/h3}\n- Names: a word with a capital first letter inside a sentence, like a boss, a zone or a player. Switch off Skip names to check them too. The first word of a sentence or a line is always checked.\n- Links, icons, markup and tokens, web and mail addresses, and lines that start with /.\n- Words in capitals (LFG, DPS), words with a number in them, and words not written in Latin letters.\n- Class names, your own characters and your tags are known words, and so are game words like aggro and dps.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Long notes{/h3}\n{p}A note longer than 20000 characters is checked only when you click Check spelling, so typing stays smooth. The marks go away when you change the text: click again to check again.{/p}\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} The lines are drawn over the text, never put in it: nothing about spelling is saved in your notes.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "note-appearance", src = "bnb-6adbc35df0ce702d", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "Note appearance",
        body = "{p}Every note can have its own look. Open Note settings {icon:@Toolbar/tb-notesettings:16}: from the note menu at the right end of the toolbar, or right-click the text > Open note settings.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}General{/h3}\n- Pin to top, Mark as favorite, Lock, and Rich note.\n- Title color: how the title shows in the note list.\n- Font and font size: the note's text in the editor, the same as picking a font on the toolbar.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Appearance{/h3}\n- Text alignment and font outline.\n- Border: a frame around the note's icon, or a plain edge with its own size, offset and brightness.\n- Icon: pick one from the game's icons, or click Random.\n- Preview shows the icon as the note list draws it.\n{p}The third tab, Situation, is about where the note shows up by itself: {link*bnbui:help.situations*Situations}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "tl-dr", src = "bnb-6adbc35e8e870641", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "writing",
        title = "tl;dr",
        body = "{p}A tl;dr is one short line about a note, like KOS or Sells mats. Give a note one in the tl;dr box above its title, or in Note settings > Situation. Pick a snippet from the list or type your own.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Where it shows{/h3}\n- Above the note title in the main window, with a button to add or change it.\n- In the game tooltip of the player or NPC the note is about: {link*bnbui:help.player-and-npc-notes*Player and NPC notes}.\n- On the note's toast when it shows up: {link*bnbui:help.toasts*Toasts}.\n{p}{link*bnbui:settings.modules.tldr*} has a checkbox for each place, and the list of snippets: change one, add your own, or put the defaults back. It also switches the small box that shows a note's tl;dr, alarm, situations and waypoints when you hover it in the note list.{/p}\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} Switching tl;dr off hides it everywhere. What you wrote stays on the notes.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "sticky-notes", src = "bnb-6ad64115f85c62f2", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "reminders",
        title = "Sticky notes",
        body = "{p}A sticky note is a note pinned to your screen as a small window, so it stays up while you play.{/p}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-sticky-note:16} Right-click a note > Open as sticky note.\n- Drag it to move it, drag an edge or a corner to resize it.\n- Each sticky has its own font, size, color, background and border.\n- A rich note shows as a rich page on its sticky.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-tasks:16} A note with tasks can show its tasks instead of its text.\n- Stickies come back where you left them after a reload.\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} Ctrl+H shows or hides every sticky, Ctrl+J brings them to the front.{/p}\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.stickies*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "situations", src = "bnb-6ad64115a9124b18", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "reminders",
        title = "Situations",
        body = "{p}{icon:@UI/ui-situation:16} A situation makes a note show up by itself where it matters: a {link*bnbui:help.toasts*toast} shows the note, or it opens as a sticky note.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}What can match{/h3}\n- A zone, a sub-zone or an instance.\n- An instance type: dungeon, raid, delve or battleground.\n- A player, an NPC or a guild.\n- A window: vendor, bank, mailbox, auction house or trainer.\n- Being rested, in an inn or a city.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Set one{/h3}\n{p}{icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-create-situation:16} Right-click a note > Create situation, or Note Settings > Situation. With nothing typed, Add uses where you are now or your target. Then pick when it shows (when it starts, when it ends, or both) and how often {icon:@UI/ui-repeat:16} (every time, once a session, once a day, once per reset, or only once). A situation can also place waypoints.{/p}\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.situations*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "toasts", src = "bnb-6ad64115295ae768", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "reminders",
        title = "Toasts",
        body = "{p}Toasts are small pop-ups on your screen: when a note's situation matches, when tasks reset, after an update.{/p}\n- Click a toast to open its note.\n- You choose which kinds show, where they appear, how they look and how long they stay.\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} Switched off, nothing pops up, but notes still match where they are set: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.toasts*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "tasks", src = "bnb-6ad64115319731a7", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "reminders",
        title = "Tasks",
        body = "{p}{icon:@UI/ui-tasks:16} Tasks are a checklist inside a note, with sub-tasks.{/p}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-create-task:16} Right-click a note > Create task, or add them in the task panel beside the note.\n- Tick a task when it is done; drag tasks to reorder them.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-reset:16} Tasks can untick themselves at the daily or weekly reset, the whole list or one task at a time: good for dailies and weekly chores.\n- A sticky note can show the note's tasks, and you can tick them there.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-tasks:16} The task button above the list shows only notes with tasks.\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.tasks*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "alarms", src = "bnb-6ad641158caa74af", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "reminders",
        title = "Alarms",
        body = "{p}An alarm on a note rings at a time you pick: a real-world time, an in-game time, or the daily or weekly reset. It can ring once or repeat on the days you choose.{/p}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-create-alarm:16} Right-click a note > Create alarm, or use the alarm button {icon:@Toolbar/tb-alarm:16} on the toolbar.\n- When it rings, the note pops up with a sound. Snooze it or dismiss it.\n- {icon:@Topbar/Normal/tp-alarms-normal:16} The alarm button at the top of the main window lists every alarm.\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.alarms*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "reference-box", src = "bnb-6ad64115b02bee55", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "in-the-world",
        title = "Reference Box",
        body = "{p}{icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-reference-box:16} The Reference Box is a panel beside the editor for the items, spells, quests and links you attach to a note.{/p}\n- Drag an item or a spell onto it, or Shift-click a link while it is open.\n- Hover an entry for its tooltip.\n- {icon:@Toolbar/tb-refbox:16} The toolbar's Reference Box button puts an entry into the text.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-model-view:16} Notes about a player keep their gear here, with a model viewer to look at it.\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.refBox*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "player-and-npc-notes", src = "bnb-6ad6411517893ab3", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "in-the-world",
        title = "Player and NPC notes",
        body = "{p}Make a note about a player or an NPC, with their details filled in.{/p}\n- A player: from the Inspect window, or their right-click menu.\n- {icon:@Search/s-icon-npc:16} An NPC: target it and press F6 (Create Note from Target).\n- The note gets their portrait and details, and for a player their gear in the {link*bnbui:help.reference-box*Reference Box}.\n- {icon:@UI/ui-tldr-add:16} Give the note a tl;dr, one short line like KOS: it shows in the game tooltip when you hover them.\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.unitNotes*} and {link*bnbui:settings.modules.tldr*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "working-with-other-addons", src = "bnb-6adbc361396d6ed0", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "in-the-world",
        title = "Working with other addons",
        body = "{p}These addons work with BigNoteBox as soon as they are installed, with no setup. {link*bnbui:settings.advanced.integrations*} shows which ones you have.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}{link*https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/bigchatbox*BigChatBox}{/h3}\n- Send a note to any chat channel line by line, or into BigChatBox's multi-line box to edit before you send it.\n- Shared notes can go out through BigChatBox too.\n- Right-click BigChatBox's chat box > Save to BigNoteBox makes a note of what you typed.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Waypoints{/h3}\n- {link*https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/tomtom*TomTom}: waypoints from your notes go to TomTom, several at once; its arrow points to the first.\n- {link*https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/mappinenhanced*MapPinEnhanced}: named pins in a BigNoteBox group, several at once.\n- {link*https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/waypointui*WaypointUI}: one waypoint at a time, through the game's map pin, with an arrow and the distance.\n{p}A situation's waypoints can be removed again when you leave: {link*bnbui:help.situations*Situations}.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Quest and gossip text{/h3}\n- {link*https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/dialogueui*DialogueUI}: its Copy Text button makes a note of the dialogue, with the quest's rewards in its Reference Box. Books work too.\n- {link*https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/immersion*Immersion}: a small Note Capture button shows during a dialogue; click it to make a note.\n{p}Both are switched on or off in {link*bnbui:settings.modules.quickNote*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "history-and-undo", src = "bnb-6ad6411504f5404f", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "keeping-notes-safe",
        title = "History and undo",
        body = "{p}BigNoteBox keeps earlier versions of your notes.{/p}\n- {icon:@Toolbar/tb-history:16} History: a version of each note is saved when you log out or reload. Compare two versions side by side and bring an old one back (right-click > History).\n- {icon:@Toolbar/tb-restore:16} Restore point: save one by hand before a big change.\n- {icon:@Toolbar/tb-undo:16} Undo: steps per note, and they can be kept between sessions.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-restore-auto:16} Rescue: a note that went missing without being deleted can be brought back from its history.\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-important:16} History and kept undo need the BigNoteBox_History addon, which comes with BigNoteBox. Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.history*} and {link*bnbui:settings.modules.undo*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "trash", src = "bnb-6ad641150aa79321", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "keeping-notes-safe",
        title = "Trash",
        body = "{p}{icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-trash:16} A deleted note goes to the Trash first, for 30 days unless you change it, so you can get it back.{/p}\n- {icon:@Topbar/Normal/tp-trash-normal:16} Open the {link*bnbui:trash*} to restore a note or delete it for good.\n- Notes older than the days you set are removed by themselves.\n- The Oracle's b prefix searches the Trash.\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-important:16} Switched off, deleting a note is permanent: {link*bnbui:settings.modules.trash*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "backup-and-import", src = "bnb-6ad64115615d93d6", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "keeping-notes-safe",
        title = "Backup and import",
        body = "{p}{link*bnbui:settings.backup*} keeps your notes safe outside the game.{/p}\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-export-json:16} Full backup: everything as JSON: your notes, templates, note tokens, tag colors and every settings profile.\n- Settings backup: every settings profile, without notes.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-export-markdown:16} Selective backup: pick the format and what goes in. Markdown is for reading outside WoW.\n{p}Copy the text and keep it in a file. To bring it back, paste it into Import on the same page. Import also takes shared notes, template codes and profile codes.{/p}\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} Notes from other note addons can be moved over from {link*bnbui:settings.backup*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "sharing-notes", src = "bnb-6ad6411532d4724d", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "keeping-notes-safe",
        title = "Sharing notes",
        body = "{p}{icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-share:16} Right-click a note > Share note.{/p}\n- Pick what goes with it: tags, tasks, Reference Box, look, situation, player or NPC data.\n- Send it straight to another player who has BigNoteBox, or copy a share code they paste into Import {icon:@Topbar/Normal/tp-import-normal:16}.\n- {icon:@ContextMenu/Symbols/cm-send-chat:16} Send to Chat posts the note's text in a chat channel, line by line.",
    },
    {
        key = "moving-from-another-notes-addon", src = "bnb-6adbc35fe81b12ee", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "keeping-notes-safe",
        title = "Moving from another notes addon",
        body = "{p}Notes you have in another notes addon can be copied into BigNoteBox. Your notes there are not touched.{/p}\n{p}{link*bnbui:settings.backup*} lists every addon it can copy from that you have installed.{/p}\n\n{div:gold-ornate}\n\n{h2}Supported as of version 2.0{/h2}\n  - Noteworthy II\n  - TakeANote\n  - Yet Another Notepad\n  - Notepad\n  - Notes\n  - TinyPad\n  - PurpleNotes\n  - SimpleNote\n  - QuickNotes\n  - OneWoW Notes\n  - MyNotepad\n  - AmmeNotepad.\n\n{div:gold-ornate}\n\n{h2}Notice{/h2}\n- Preview shows what will come over before anything is copied.\n- Migrate Now copies the notes, then reloads the UI.\n- TakeANote: its categories can become tags on the notes.\n- Notes kept per character come over for the character you are logged in with. Log in with each character to bring theirs.\n\n{p}When BigNoteBox finds one of these addons at login, it offers to copy the notes. Don't ask again stops the offer; the button on the Backup page stays.{/p}\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} While you have notes, BigNoteBox offers to make a backup first: {link*bnbui:help.backup-and-import*Backup and import}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "settings-profiles", src = "bnb-6ad64115eb5bb497", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "setting-up",
        title = "Settings profiles",
        body = "{p}{icon:@Topbar/Normal/tp-settings-normal:16} A profile is a set of settings and window layout. Each character picks one; your notes are the same in every profile.{/p}\n- Make a new profile as a copy of the current one, or from scratch.\n- Export a profile as a code to share or keep; Import one from a code.\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-important:16} Picking another profile reloads the UI.{/p}\n{p}Settings: {link*bnbui:settings.advanced*}.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "modules", src = "bnb-6ad64115b2bb4cac", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "setting-up",
        title = "Modules",
        body = "{p}Most parts of BigNoteBox are modules you can switch on or off in {link*bnbui:settings.modules*}. Switching one off hides it everywhere. Your notes keep everything that belongs to it, so switching it back on brings it all back.{/p}\n{p:c}{icon:@UI/ui-mode-minimal:64} {icon:@UI/ui-mode-full:64} {icon:@UI/ui-mode-custom:64}{/p}\n{p}Minimal, Full and Custom at the top of that page switch many at once. The {link*bnbui:wizard*setup wizard} asks the same on your first login.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "keys-and-commands", src = "bnb-6ad6411580f66ca0", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "setting-up",
        title = "Keys and commands",
        body = "{h3}Keys{/h3}\n- Ctrl+N: open or close BigNoteBox.\n- F8: new note. F7: quick note. F6: note from your target.\n- Ctrl+Space: Oracle search.\n- Ctrl+H: show or hide every sticky. Ctrl+J: bring stickies to the front.\n{p}{icon:@Documentation/doc-info:16} A key the game or another addon already uses is left alone. Change them in {link*bnbui:settings.general*}.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Commands{/h3}\n- /bnb: open or close the window.\n- /bnb new: a new note.\n- /bnb search text: Oracle search.\n- /bnb config: Settings.\n- /bnb whatsnew: the latest patch notes.\n- /bnb help: this help book.\n- /bnb commands: every command in chat.",
    },
    {
        key = "look-and-feel", src = "bnb-6adbc35cc066d29f", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "setting-up",
        title = "Look and feel",
        body = "{p}BigNoteBox has two looks: the normal look, in the game's own frames, and skin mode, a dark window of its own in the colors of a skin preset. Both are set in {link*bnbui:settings.appearance*}.{/p}\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Skin mode{/h3}\n- Tick Enable skin mode, then reload the UI when it asks.\n- Pick a skin preset, and set its brightness and the window's opacity.\n- Randomize theme gives you a new preset at every login or reload.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Text{/h3}\n- Note font and Note body font size change the text of your notes.\n- Pick WoW's default font when your notes are in Chinese or Korean: the other fonts do not have those characters.\n- Load LibSharedMedia fonts adds the fonts of your other addons to the list.\n{h3}The note list and dates{/h3}\n- Note list display mode: Normal, Compact (small icons, no preview) or Spacious (big icons, three preview lines).\n- Timestamp format: relative (2 days ago) or a date. You can also pick a 24-hour clock, and server time instead of your own.\n{div:gold-ornate}\n{h3}Motion{/h3}\n{p}{link*bnbui:settings.modules.accessibility*} sets how sticky notes move when you hide or show them all: how long it takes, how big they grow as they fade, and how the text fades. Switch it off for no animation.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "right-click-menu", src = "bnb-6adbc360447f0654", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = "setting-up",
        title = "Right-click menu",
        body = "{p}Right-click a note for its menu. A main item, like Copy or Share, opens a sub-menu when you rest the pointer on it.{/p}\n{p}{link*bnbui:settings.modules.contextMenu*} sets what a click on a main item does:{/p}\n- Pick one entry from the item's sub-menu: a click on the item runs it, and the item takes its name.\n- Or pick Only open the sub-menu.\n{p}Open delay sets how long the pointer rests on an item before its sub-menu opens. Try it opens a sample menu with your settings; its entries do nothing.{/p}",
    },
    {
        key = "glossary", src = "bnb-6ae48f586169b134", rich = true, clients = nil, chapter = nil, back = true,
        title = "Glossary",
        body = "{p}The words BigNoteBox uses, A-Z. Click a word for the topic that tells the whole story.{/p}\n{h3}A{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:settings.modules.accessibility*Accessibility}: Settings for motion: how sticky notes move when they hide and show, and smooth scrolling.\n- {link*bnbui:help.alarms*Alarm}: A time set on a note. When it comes, the note pops up with a sound; it can ring once or repeat on the days you pick.\n{h3}B{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.working-with-other-addons*BigChatBox}: A chat addon by the same author. Send notes to chat line by line through it, or keep what you typed as a note.\n{h3}C{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.getting-started*Character note}: A note that belongs to one character only. Its opposite is a Global note.\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-list*Custom sort}: Your own order for the notes, made by dragging them.\n{h3}D{/h3}\n- {col:ffd200}Danger Zone{/col}: The window for big resets and deletes: settings, the Trash, history, all notes, dictionary words, text shortcuts or everything at once. Each one waits for a countdown first.\n- {link*bnbui:help.spelling*Dictionary}: Your own words, added from a red-marked word's right-click menu, so the spellchecker accepts them.\n{h3}E{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.explorer-view*Explorer view}: Your notes and folders as a grid of icons over the whole main window, like the file explorer on your computer.\n- {link*bnbui:help.backup-and-import*Export}: Saving notes outside the game: as JSON to bring back in later, as Markdown to read, or a note as a web page.\n{h3}F{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-list*Favorite}: A note marked with the star. The Explorer view can show favorites first, and the Oracle finds them with *.\n- {link*bnbui:features*Features}: The Help book's tab with everything BigNoteBox can do, A-Z.\n- {link*bnbui:help.sticky-notes*Focus look}: A sticky note that hides everything but its text and background.\n- {link*bnbui:help.focus-mode*Focus mode}: Writing in full screen, with the game interface hidden and the camera slowly turning around your character.\n- {link*bnbui:help.folders*Folder}: A place to keep notes together, in the note list and the Explorer view. Deleting a folder never deletes its notes.\n- {link*bnbui:help.backup-and-import*Full backup}: Everything in one JSON text: notes, templates, tokens, tag colors and every settings profile.\n{h3}G{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.getting-started*Global note}: A note every character on your account sees. Its opposite is a Character note.\n{h3}H{/h3}\n- {col:ffd200}Help book{/col}: This window: the help topics, the Features tab and the patch notes. Open it with the Help button at the top or /bnb help.\n- {link*bnbui:help.history-and-undo*History}: Earlier versions of a note, saved when you log out or reload. Compare two and bring one back.\n{h3}I{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-appearance*Icon frame}: The frame drawn around a note's icon, like the round glass orb on player notes.\n- {link*bnbui:help.backup-and-import*Import}: Brings in a backup, a shared note, a template code or a profile code. It adds beside what you have and never overwrites.\n{h3}L{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.writing-notes*Locked note}: A note that cannot be changed until you unlock it.\n{h3}M{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.rich-notes*Markup}: The tags a rich note is written with, for headings, colors, icons and links. The Markup tab shows them; the toolbar puts them in for you.\n- {link*bnbui:help.modules*Minimal, Full and Custom}: The three choices at the top of Settings > Modules that switch many modules on or off at once.\n- {link*bnbui:help.getting-started*Minimap button}: The BigNoteBox button on the minimap: click to open, drag to move.\n- {link*bnbui:help.reference-box*Model viewer}: The Reference Box's 3D view of a player or NPC, with a transmog view for player gear.\n- {link*bnbui:help.modules*Module}: A part of BigNoteBox you can switch on or off. Switched off, it is hidden, and your notes keep everything that belongs to it.\n- {link*bnbui:help.moving-from-another-notes-addon*Moving notes over}: Copying your notes from another notes addon into BigNoteBox. Nothing is removed from the other addon.\n{h3}N{/h3}\n- {col:ffd200}NEW{/col}: The green mark in Settings on everything new in this version.\n- {link*bnbui:help.quick-notes*Note Capture}: The note button on quest, gossip, book and letter windows: one click keeps their text as a note.\n- {link*bnbui:help.links-in-notes*Note link}: A link in a note that opens another note. It keeps working when that note is renamed.\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-list*Note list}: The list of your notes on the left of the main window.\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-appearance*Note settings}: A note's own look: icon, icon frame, border, background and font, and its situation.\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-tokens*Note token}: A word in double braces that BigNoteBox fills in for you: the date, your zone, your character's name and more.\n- {link*bnbui:help.player-and-npc-notes*NPC note}: A note about an NPC, made by targeting it and pressing F6. It gets the NPC's portrait.\n{h3}O{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.oracle-search*Oracle search}: The search bar that finds any note from anywhere in the game (Ctrl+Space).\n{h3}P{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:whatsnew*Patch notes}: What changed in each version of BigNoteBox, a tab in the Help book.\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-list*Pinned note}: A note kept at the top of the list.\n- {link*bnbui:help.player-and-npc-notes*Player note}: A note about a player, from the Inspect window or their right-click menu. It keeps their gear.\n- {link*bnbui:help.oracle-search*Prefix}: A letter before your words in the Oracle bar that narrows the search, like p for player notes or t for tasks.\n- {link*bnbui:help.settings-profiles*Profile}: A set of settings and window positions. Each character picks one; your notes are the same in every profile.\n{h3}Q{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.quick-notes*Quick note}: A note made in a hurry with F7, in the main window or as a sticky note.\n{h3}R{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.reference-box*Reference Box}: The panel beside a note for the items, spells, quests and links you attach to it.\n- {link*bnbui:help.history-and-undo*Rescue}: Brings back a note that went missing without being deleted, from its last known state.\n- {link*bnbui:help.tasks*Reset}: The game's daily and weekly reset. Tasks can untick themselves then, and alarms can ring.\n- {link*bnbui:help.history-and-undo*Restore point}: A version of a note you save by hand before a big change.\n- {link*bnbui:help.rich-notes*Rich note}: A note with headings, colors, icons, pictures and links, shown as a small page.\n- {link*bnbui:help.right-click-menu*Right-click menu}: Every action a note has, from a right-click on it. You choose what a click on a main entry does.\n{h3}S{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.getting-started*Scope}: Whether a note is Global or belongs to one character.\n- {link*bnbui:help.sharing-notes*Send to Chat}: Posts a note's text in a chat channel, line by line.\n- {link*bnbui:help.backup-and-import*Settings backup}: Every settings profile as one JSON text, without notes.\n- {link*bnbui:help.modules*Setup wizard}: The questions on your first login that pick your modules and look.\n- {link*bnbui:help.sharing-notes*Share code}: A note packed into text you can give another player, who pastes it into Import.\n- {link*bnbui:help.situations*Situation}: Where or when a note shows up by itself: a zone, an instance, a player or NPC, a vendor or bank window, being rested and more.\n- {link*bnbui:help.look-and-feel*Skin mode}: BigNoteBox's second look: a dark window of its own in the colors of a skin preset.\n- {link*bnbui:settings.modules.accessibility*Smooth scrolling}: The mouse wheel glides instead of jumping. Speed and distance are yours to set.\n- {link*bnbui:help.alarms*Snooze}: Puts off a ringing alarm for a while.\n- {link*bnbui:help.spelling*Spellchecker}: Marks words it does not know with a red line as you type; right-click one for suggestions.\n- {link*bnbui:help.sticky-notes*Sticky note}: A note pinned to your screen as a small window, so it stays up while you play.\n- {link*bnbui:help.tasks*Sub-task}: A task inside another task.\n{h3}T{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.tags*Tag}: A short word on a note, like Raid or Gold, to find and group notes by.\n- {link*bnbui:help.tags*Tag Manager}: The window that renames, colors and deletes tags across all your notes.\n- {link*bnbui:help.tags*Tag tree}: Every note grouped by its tags, one branch per tag.\n- {link*bnbui:help.tasks*Task}: A line in a note's checklist. Tick it when it is done.\n- {link*bnbui:help.note-templates*Template}: A ready-made start for a new note: title, text, tags and look.\n- {link*bnbui:help.spelling*Text shortcut}: A short word that turns into longer text as you type, like brb into be right back.\n- {link*bnbui:help.tl-dr*tl;dr}: One short line about a note, like KOS or Sells mats, shown under its title and in tooltips.\n- {link*bnbui:help.toasts*Toast}: A small pop-up on your screen: a note whose situation matches, a task reset, an update.\n- {link*bnbui:help.trash*Trash}: Where a deleted note waits, 30 days unless you change it, so you can get it back.\n{h3}U{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.history-and-undo*Undo}: Steps back in a note, per note, and they can be kept between sessions.\n{h3}V{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.rich-notes*View mode}: A rich note shown as a page. Edit mode shows its markup to change it.\n{h3}W{/h3}\n- {link*bnbui:help.links-in-notes*Waypoint}: A pin on the map to a place. Notes hold them as links, and a situation can place them for you.",
    },
}
